5. Significant incidents, near misses and lessons applied
Injury and incident records remain important. They explain what has happened and support investigation.

However, the absence of a reported injury does not establish that every significant risk is controlled.

A leadership dashboard should help reviewers distinguish actual consequences from potential consequences, using an agreed assessment method. It should also show whether investigation actions have been implemented and whether lessons apply elsewhere.

